# Coding patterns and conventions

Agent policy (always wins)
- Do not build, start the dev server, typecheck, migrate, deploy, commit, or run/add tests unless the user explicitly asks — see `.cursor/rules/00-global-safety.mdc` and `05-workflow-execution.mdc`.
- Checklists below are for humans / when the user requests those steps.

TypeScript and style
- TypeScript everywhere; keep strictness aligned with repo configs
- Follow existing patterns in the file you edit; prefer small, focused changes

API endpoints (app/server/api)
- File naming encodes HTTP method: foo.get.ts, bar.post.ts, item/[id].patch.ts, etc.
- Validate input with Zod (app/schema/zod.ts or feature-specific schema files under app/schema/)
- Use server/middleware/auth.ts for protected routes; requireAdmin.ts for admin-only
- Wrap handlers with error helpers when applicable:
  - withErrorHandler.ts for standardized try/catch
  - handleApiError.ts and plaidApiError.ts for integration error normalization
- Access persistence via server/clients/prismaClient.ts; avoid creating ad-hoc clients in routes
- Delegate nontrivial logic to server/services/*; keep routes thin

Services
- Place domain logic in server/services/*; keep a clear public method surface
- For forecast engine features, prefer extending modules under server/services/forecast/* rather than ad-hoc math in routes
- Use server/lib helpers for cross-cutting needs (queueManager, pagination, notifications, audit logs, etc.)

Data validation and schemas
- Central schemas live in app/schema/zod.ts with targeted files like app/schema/plaid.ts and app/schema/reconciliation.ts
- When introducing new DTOs, colocate schema with feature or extend zod.ts thoughtfully

Encryption and secrets
- Many Prisma fields are annotated with /// @encrypted (see app/prisma/schema.prisma)
- Never `in`/`contains` on encrypted fields — `.cursor/rules/encrypted-prisma-queries.mdc` and encryption-and-keys.mdc
- Use server/services/RsaService.ts, server/lib/plaidAccessTokenCrypto.ts helpers when handling secrets
- Never log plaintext secrets or sensitive PII

Queues and cron
- Define BullMQ queues in app/server/queues/*; use server/lib/queueManager.ts
- Schedule recurring tasks via app/server/cron/* with nuxt-cron

Naming
- Endpoints: kabab-case resources, nested folders reflect URL segments
- Services: <Domain>Service.ts (e.g., PlaidSyncService, NotificationCenterService)
- Tests: mirror source structure (e.g., server/services/foo/__tests__/Foo.test.ts)

# Safe change checklists (when the user asks)

Schema changes (Prisma)
- Edit app/prisma/schema.prisma (and microservice schema if shared tables change)
- Prefer asking the user to create a **manual migration**; agents must not run `prisma migrate dev` / `db push` unless explicitly requested (backend-best-practices.mdc)
- Ensure decimal precision is appropriate for money fields (Decimal(19,2) common)
- Respect field encryption annotations; do not remove /// @encrypted unless intended
- When the user asks: regenerate client (`prisma generate`), update seeds if needed

API changes
- Update or add Zod schemas
- Keep handler thin; delegate to service
- Add/extend unit tests only when the user asks
- Check auth coverage and admin guards

Forecast engine
- Prefer extending existing modules (AccountRegisterService, ReoccurrenceService, TransferService, LoanCalculatorService, etc.)
- When the user asks for tests:
  - pnpm test:forecast:unit
  - pnpm test:forecast:integration
  - pnpm test:forecast (scenario runner)

Background jobs
- For new periodic behavior, prefer:
  - Queue worker in app/server/queues/* if asynchronous work is needed
  - Cron under app/server/cron/* to trigger or orchestrate
- Ensure idempotency and observability (logs, IntegrationJobLog if relevant)

Security and auth
- Enforce authentication middleware; prefer per-endpoint authorization checks via accountMembership.ts, accountAccess.ts, requireAdmin.ts
- Use rateLimitRedis.ts for abuse-prone endpoints
- Handle MFA and passkeys via existing endpoints flows (mfa/*, two-factor-auth.ts)

Errors and responses
- Normalize API errors to userFriendlyApiError.ts when surfacing to the UI
- Log integration failures through recordIntegrationJobLog.ts or recordPlaidSyncLog.ts

Testing
- Agents: do not add or run tests unless the user asks
- When adding tests (user-requested): unit near the code; API under app/server/api/__tests__; e2e under app/tests/e2e

CI and deployment
- PRs run lint/test, build images, and deploy to staging if from the main repo
- Default branch builds + deploys to production
- Use .deploy/dineros.template.yaml for k8s resource references when reasoning about env vars
- Agents: do not deploy unless the user asks
